### Describe the bug and add attachments

OrderConfirmationController and GuestTrackingController can transform guest into customer, but both don't check if provided email already exists during POST request, allowing for two customers to have same email address which leads to one account being unable to log in

### Expected behavior

OrderConfirmationController and GuestTrackingController need to check if customer with the same mail address exists during POST request. Adding first 'if' resolves the problem:

```php
//added in 'postProcess()'
if ($this->customer->is_guest == 1 && Customer::customerExists($this->customer->email)) {
    $this->errors[] = $this->trans(
        'An account was already registered with this email address',
        [],
        'Shop.Notifications.Error'
    );
} elseif ($this->customer->is_guest == 0) {
    $this->errors[] = $this->trans(
        'A customer account has already been created from this guest account. Please sign in.',
        [],
        'Shop.Notifications.Error'
    );
// Attempt to convert the customer
} elseif ($this->customer->transformToCustomer($this->context->language->id, $password)) {
    $this->success[] = $this->trans(
        'Your guest account has been successfully transformed into a customer account. You can now log in as a registered shopper.',
        [],
        'Shop.Notifications.Success'
    );
}
```

